{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01315",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.38,
      "end_seconds": 5.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Erm, hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.15,
      "end_seconds": 11.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.57,
      "end_seconds": 21.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "Um, so... a dry cough in the evenings. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.44,
      "end_seconds": 25.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "how long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.95,
      "end_seconds": 37.96,
      "duration_seconds": 11.01,
      "text": "about... well, four weeks. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. It's the not knowing that gets to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.79,
      "end_seconds": 44.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.25,
      "end_seconds": 48.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Not to to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.82,
      "end_seconds": 52.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.8,
      "end_seconds": 60.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "An irregular heartbeat, for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.39,
      "end_seconds": 68.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "Right, so an irregular heartbeat is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.32,
      "end_seconds": 86.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.08,
      "end_seconds": 91.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.62,
      "end_seconds": 94.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "what's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.85,
      "end_seconds": 100.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.19,
      "end_seconds": 104.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.82,
      "end_seconds": 107.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "I swim twice a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.08,
      "end_seconds": 111.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.87,
      "end_seconds": 116.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.46,
      "end_seconds": 132.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "And what about shortness of breath, wheeze or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.03,
      "end_seconds": 137.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "no, no shortness of breath, wheeze or fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.32,
      "end_seconds": 140.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.17,
      "end_seconds": 143.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.6,
      "end_seconds": 150.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "let me get the readings out of the way"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.26,
      "end_seconds": 167.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.98,
      "end_seconds": 196.19,
      "duration_seconds": 11.21,
      "text": "okay: temp 36.7 degrees respiratory rate 15. And And SpO2 97 percent on room air heart rate 72 BP is 123 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.16,
      "end_seconds": 200.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "ah is that alright doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.05,
      "end_seconds": 205.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.57,
      "end_seconds": 212.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.94,
      "end_seconds": 215.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.99,
      "end_seconds": 229.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Your chest is clear and your nose looks a little swollen inside."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.15,
      "end_seconds": 232.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.75,
      "end_seconds": 236.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "all finished thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.83,
      "end_seconds": 266.44,
      "duration_seconds": 14.61,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with seasonal hay fever causing the cough. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.79,
      "end_seconds": 271.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "actually, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.26,
      "end_seconds": 280.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like seasonal hay fever causing the cough"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.45,
      "end_seconds": 318.17,
      "duration_seconds": 22.72,
      "text": "I'm prescribing fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, for the season. That's for hay fever. Keep windows closed on high-pollen days and wash your hair at night. If you start wheezing, that's the point to come in urgently. I'll want another look in a month. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.91,
      "end_seconds": 321.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "thank you, doctor, goodbye"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.29,
      "end_seconds": 324.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}